---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import LeadForm from '../components/LeadForm.astro';

const faqs = [
	{
		question: 'How do I choose a fractional CMO near me?',
		answer:
			'Prioritize experience over proximity. Look for real operating experience in your revenue range — $5M–$50M looks nothing like enterprise — specific, measurable results at similar companies, and someone senior enough to lead your team. Then treat location as a tiebreaker. A strong fractional CMO an hour away beats a mediocre one down the street.',
	},
	{
		question: 'What does a fractional CMO cost per month?',
		answer:
			'Most fractional CMO engagements in the US run $3,000–$15,000 per month depending on scope and time commitment — a fraction of the $150,000–$300,000 a full-time CMO costs each year once salary, benefits, bonuses, and overhead are included. SumoLab scopes each engagement around your goals and stage, so you pay only for the level of leadership you need.',
	},
	{
		question: 'Do fractional CMOs work in person or remotely?',
		answer:
			'Both. Most of the work — strategy, weekly leadership sessions, team direction — happens remotely, which is why fit matters more than proximity. Because SumoLab is based in Chandler, Arizona, Phoenix-metro clients can meet in person whenever it helps; clients elsewhere in the country work with Jerry on the same weekly rhythm, over video.',
	},
	{
		question: 'What happens in the first 90 days with a fractional CMO?',
		answer:
			'Expect a deep dive into the business first: revenue model, sales process, current marketing, and team. From there, a prioritized strategy with clear KPIs and a weekly working cadence. By day 90 you should have a plan your leadership team can defend — and early wins already in motion.',
	},
	{
		question: 'What areas does SumoLab serve?',
		answer:
			'SumoLab serves the Phoenix metro in person — Chandler, Phoenix, Scottsdale, Tempe, Mesa, and Gilbert — and businesses across Arizona and the US through remote engagements. Wherever you are, the place to start is a short intro call to see whether the fit is right.',
	},
];

const structuredData = [
	{
		'@context': 'https://schema.org',
		'@type': 'ProfessionalService',
		name: 'SumoLab',
		description:
			'Fractional CMO services for established businesses generating $5M–$50M in annual revenue. Based in Chandler, Arizona — serving the Phoenix metro in person and clients nationwide remotely.',
		url: 'https://sumolab.co/fractional-cmo-near-me/',
		telephone: '+14808269400',
		email: 'jerry@sumolab.co',
		address: {
			'@type': 'PostalAddress',
			addressLocality: 'Chandler',
			addressRegion: 'AZ',
			addressCountry: 'US',
		},
		founder: {
			'@type': 'Person',
			name: 'Jerry Suhrstedt',
			jobTitle: 'Founder & Fractional CMO',
			sameAs: 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/jerrysuhrstedt/',
		},
		areaServed: [
			{ '@type': 'City', name: 'Phoenix' },
			{ '@type': 'City', name: 'Scottsdale' },
			{ '@type': 'City', name: 'Chandler' },
			{ '@type': 'City', name: 'Tempe' },
			{ '@type': 'City', name: 'Mesa' },
			{ '@type': 'City', name: 'Gilbert' },
			{ '@type': 'State', name: 'Arizona' },
			{ '@type': 'Country', name: 'United States' },
		],
	},
	{
		'@context': 'https://schema.org',
		'@type': 'FAQPage',
		mainEntity: faqs.map((faq) => ({
			'@type': 'Question',
			name: faq.question,
			acceptedAnswer: {
				'@type': 'Answer',
				text: faq.answer,
			},
		})),
	},
];
---

<Layout
	title="Fractional CMO Near Me — Phoenix, Arizona | SumoLab"
	description="Searching for a fractional CMO near me? SumoLab's Jerry Suhrstedt brings 26 years of experience to Phoenix-area businesses — in person or remote nationwide."
	structuredData={structuredData}
>
	<PageHero
		image="/photos/services-hero-leadership.jpg"
		mobileImage="/photos/services-hero-leadership-mobile.jpg"
		imageAlt="Jerry Suhrstedt of SumoLab leading a marketing strategy session for a Phoenix-area business"
		eyebrow="Fractional CMO Near Me"
		align="left"
		imagePosition="75% center"
	>
		<h1>Searching &ldquo;fractional CMO near me&rdquo;? Start here.</h1>
		<p>If you searched for a fractional CMO near me, here's the direct answer: SumoLab is a fractional CMO practice led by Jerry Suhrstedt, based in Chandler, Arizona, with 26 years of marketing and business-building experience across twelve companies. Jerry works in person with businesses across Phoenix, Scottsdale, Tempe, Mesa, and Gilbert — and remotely with clients nationwide.</p>
	</PageHero>

	<Section tone="white">
		<div class="two-col" style="align-items:start;gap:64px">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow-label"><span class="dot"></span>In-person vs. remote</p>
				<h2 class="page-h2">Does location actually matter?</h2>
				<p class="lede" style="margin-top:24px">For fractional CMO work, proximity matters far less than fit, experience, and the quality of leadership. Most of what the role covers — strategy, positioning, pipeline reviews, leading your marketing team — happens in scheduled working sessions that are every bit as effective over video as across a conference table. The best fractional engagements I've run were built on trust, results, and clear communication — not a shared zip code.</p>
				<p class="lede" style="margin-top:16px">So before you filter candidates by city, ask the harder questions: does this person have operating experience deep enough to understand your business? Have they built companies, not just managed campaigns? Can they sit at your leadership table and make decisions that move revenue? That's what you're hiring for — see what a full <a href="/services/fractional-cmo/">fractional CMO engagement</a> actually covers before you decide.</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow-label"><span class="dot"></span>Service area</p>
				<h2 class="page-h2">Chandler-based. Valley-wide. Nationwide.</h2>
				<p class="lede" style="margin-top:24px">SumoLab is based in Chandler, in the heart of the East Valley, and serves the entire Phoenix metro in person — Phoenix, Scottsdale, Tempe, Mesa, Gilbert, and the surrounding cities. When a strategy session, leadership offsite, or team workshop works better face to face, it's a short drive across the Valley, not a flight.</p>
				<p class="lede" style="margin-top:16px">Beyond Arizona, engagements run remotely with businesses across the US on the same weekly cadence: clear priorities, direct access, and no waiting on geography. And if you're not sure you need a full CMO yet, some teams are better served by a <a href="/services/fractional-marketing-director/">fractional marketing director</a> — a conversation will make the distinction clear.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</Section>

	<Section tone="plain">
		<p class="eyebrow-label"><span class="dot"></span>What to look for</p>
		<h2 class="page-h2">How to choose a fractional CMO near you.</h2>
		<p class="lede" style="margin-top:24px;max-width:680px">Whether you're comparing Phoenix-area candidates or a shortlist from across the country, the evaluation criteria are the same. Three questions separate operators from theorists.</p>
		<div class="questions-grid" style="margin-top:40px">
			<div class="question-card">
				<h3 class="page-h3">Have they actually run a business?</h3>
				<p class="lede">Marketing strategy from someone who's only ever been inside a marketing department is different from strategy from someone who's owned the P&L. Ask specifically: have they founded or co-founded a company? Carried a number? Made payroll? The answer changes everything about how they'll think about your marketing.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="question-card">
				<h3 class="page-h3">Do they know your revenue range?</h3>
				<p class="lede">Enterprise CMO experience doesn't automatically translate to the $5M–$50M world. The strategies, the resource constraints, the need to do more with less — these are genuinely different. Look for someone who's navigated that range before, not someone coming down from a Fortune 500 to figure it out on your dime.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="question-card">
				<h3 class="page-h3">Can they show you real results?</h3>
				<p class="lede">Ask for specific examples: a company they worked with at a similar stage, the problem they walked into, the measurable outcome. Not "we improved brand awareness." Revenue growth. Lead volume. Cost per acquisition. That's the standard SumoLab holds itself to — the <a href="/case-studies/">case studies</a> show the actual numbers.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</Section>

	<Section tone="ink">
		<p class="eyebrow-label" style="color:var(--orange-400)"><span class="dot"></span>What SumoLab brings</p>
		<h2 class="page-h2" style="color:#fff">26 years of building and marketing real businesses.</h2>
		<p class="lede" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.85);max-width:680px;margin-top:24px">I've founded and co-founded twelve companies. Taken a home building business from bankruptcy to $12M. Grown a builder from 60 homes a year to over 800. Taken another from $3M to $11M in under three years. The marketing strategies I bring to your business have been tested under real conditions, with real stakes — not in a classroom or a consulting deck.</p>
		<p class="lede" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.85);max-width:680px;margin-top:16px">Every fractional CMO engagement starts with understanding your business first and your marketing second. That order matters. The strategy follows from the business, not the other way around. When you're ready to <a href="/">hire a fractional CMO</a>, that's the standard to hold every candidate to — including me.</p>
	</Section>

	<Section tone="white">
		<p class="eyebrow-label"><span class="dot"></span>Common questions</p>
		<h2 class="page-h2">What business owners ask before hiring.</h2>
		<div class="divider-rows" style="margin-top:40px">
			<div>
				<h3 class="page-h3">How do I choose a fractional CMO near me?</h3>
				<p class="lede" style="margin-top:12px">Prioritize experience over proximity. Look for real operating experience in your revenue range — $5M–$50M looks nothing like enterprise — specific, measurable results at similar companies, and someone senior enough to lead your team. Then treat location as a tiebreaker. A strong fractional CMO an hour away beats a mediocre one down the street.</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<h3 class="page-h3">What does a fractional CMO cost per month?</h3>
				<p class="lede" style="margin-top:12px">Most fractional CMO engagements in the US run $3,000–$15,000 per month depending on scope and time commitment — a fraction of the $150,000–$300,000 a full-time CMO costs each year once salary, benefits, bonuses, and overhead are included. SumoLab scopes each engagement around your goals and stage, so you pay only for the level of leadership you need.</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<h3 class="page-h3">Do fractional CMOs work in person or remotely?</h3>
				<p class="lede" style="margin-top:12px">Both. Most of the work — strategy, weekly leadership sessions, team direction — happens remotely, which is why fit matters more than proximity. Because SumoLab is based in Chandler, Arizona, Phoenix-metro clients can meet in person whenever it helps; clients elsewhere in the country work with Jerry on the same weekly rhythm, over video.</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<h3 class="page-h3">What happens in the first 90 days with a fractional CMO?</h3>
				<p class="lede" style="margin-top:12px">Expect a deep dive into the business first: revenue model, sales process, current marketing, and team. From there, a prioritized strategy with clear KPIs and a weekly working cadence. By day 90 you should have a plan your leadership team can defend — and early wins already in motion.</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<h3 class="page-h3">What areas does SumoLab serve?</h3>
				<p class="lede" style="margin-top:12px">SumoLab serves the Phoenix metro in person — Chandler, Phoenix, Scottsdale, Tempe, Mesa, and Gilbert — and businesses across Arizona and the US through remote engagements. Wherever you are, the place to start is a short <a href="/contact/">intro call</a> to see whether the fit is right.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="card-cta-row" style="margin-top:56px">
			<h2 class="page-h2" style="margin:0">Not sure if this is the right fit? One conversation will make it clear.</h2>
			<LeadForm />
		</div>
	</Section>
</Layout>

<style>
	.questions-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
		gap: 32px;
	}
	.question-card {
		border-top: 3px solid var(--orange-500);
		padding-top: 20px;
	}
	@media (max-width: 780px) {
		.questions-grid {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
	}
</style>
